{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"323ac2d47ebd92f4","name":"card_unit_jagdpanzer_iv","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Germany/NavalWarfare/units/card_unit_jagdpanzer_iv","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"JAGDPANZER IV","text":"When you attack and destroy an enemy unit, Convert a random card in the enemy hand into PRODUCTION.","flavorText":"The Jagdpanzer IV was a German tank destroyer developed during World War II, based on the Panzer IV chassis. Designed to provide a low-profile, heavily armored vehicle for anti-tank operations, it was produced from December 1943 to April 1945, with approximately 2,000 units built. Initially, the Jagdpanzer IV was armed with a 7.5cm PaK 39 L/48 gun. Later versions, known as the Panzer IV/70, were equipped with the more powerful 7.5cm PaK 42 L/70 gun. The vehicle featured sloped armor up to 80 mm thick and had a four-man crew. Its low silhouette and strong frontal armor made it effective in ambush roles. The Jagdpanzer IV served on both the Eastern and Western Fronts, participating in battles such as Normandy and the Ardennes Offensive. While effective as a tank destroyer, it performed less well when used as a substitute for tanks or assault guns, roles for which it was not originally intended.","faction":"Germany","type":"tank","rarity":"Rare","cost":3,"operationCost":2,"attack":4,"defense":4},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_jagdpanzer_iv","title":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_jagdpanzer_iv_title","SourceString":"JAGDPANZER IV","LocalizedString":"JAGDPANZER IV"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::tank","attack":4,"defense":4,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Germany","kredits":3,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_jagdpanzer_iv_text","SourceString":"When you attack and destroy an enemy unit, Convert a random card in the enemy hand into PRODUCTION.","LocalizedString":"When you attack and destroy an enemy unit, Convert a random card in the enemy hand into PRODUCTION."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_jagdpanzer_iv_history","SourceString":"The Jagdpanzer IV was a German tank destroyer developed during World War II, based on the Panzer IV chassis. Designed to provide a low-profile, heavily armored vehicle for anti-tank operations, it was produced from December 1943 to April 1945, with approximately 2,000 units built. Initially, the Jagdpanzer IV was armed with a 7.5cm PaK 39 L/48 gun. Later versions, known as the Panzer IV/70, were equipped with the more powerful 7.5cm PaK 42 L/70 gun. The vehicle featured sloped armor up to 80 mm thick and had a four-man crew. Its low silhouette and strong frontal armor made it effective in ambush roles. The Jagdpanzer IV served on both the Eastern and Western Fronts, participating in battles such as Normandy and the Ardennes Offensive. While effective as a tank destroyer, it performed less well when used as a substitute for tanks or assault guns, roles for which it was not originally intended.","LocalizedString":"The Jagdpanzer IV was a German tank destroyer developed during World War II, based on the Panzer IV chassis. Designed to provide a low-profile, heavily armored vehicle for anti-tank operations, it was produced from December 1943 to April 1945, with approximately 2,000 units built. Initially, the Jagdpanzer IV was armed with a 7.5cm PaK 39 L/48 gun. Later versions, known as the Panzer IV/70, were equipped with the more powerful 7.5cm PaK 42 L/70 gun. The vehicle featured sloped armor up to 80 mm thick and had a four-man crew. Its low silhouette and strong frontal armor made it effective in ambush roles. The Jagdpanzer IV served on both the Eastern and Western Fronts, participating in battles such as Normandy and the Ardennes Offensive. While effective as a tank destroyer, it performed less well when used as a substitute for tanks or assault guns, roles for which it was not originally intended."},"operationCost":2,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","cardSet":"ECardSetEn